>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Use carpets and rugs made from 'breathable' materials \(such as woven fabric\), avoiding carpets and rugs with solid rubber or vinyl backings that could trap moisture under the material.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( You should also ensure that the underside of the carpets and rugs is kept clean and free from abrasives that could damage your floors.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( Use mats or rugs at entrances to minimise dirt and moisture from being tracked inside. At entrances, mats and rugs should be laid both externally and internally.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 105 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
>>
endobj
